In the past few years more and more systems have been installed at mushroom farms using vacuum cooling as a rapid cooling method for mushrooms. Having the correct cooling processes in place is important in the handling of any fresh produce but for mushrooms it can be even more critical.
Vacuum cooling is a rapid and more efficient alternative to traditional atmospheric or ambient cooling. It is a relatively new technology based on reducing the difference between ambient atmospheric pressure and water vapor pressure in a product.
Vacuum cooling is widely used in the fresh food industry in the United States, Europe and China. Since water evaporates at low pressure and consumes energy, it can effectively reduce the temperature of fresh produce from the field temperature of 28°C to 2°C.
