Cambodian youth one step closer to skills, jobs
Phnom Penh, Cambodia – Youth in Cambodia are one step closer to gaining professional culinary experience and expanding their work opportunities. With the Academy of Culinary Arts in Cambodia,
Cambodia’s public and private sectors have come together to create the nation’s first Public-Private Partnership and aim to change the face of the hospitality sector.
The Academy and SHL Join Forces for Global Education
Youth in Cambodia are closer than ever to professional culinary experience and international work opportunities as the Academy
Register today to start your career in the culinary arts
The Academy of Culinary Arts Cambodia (ACAC) is a hospitality training institution that offers its students an internationally recognized higher diploma/associate degree in the culinary arts. The Academy provides instruction in Khmer and English to students who have completed secondary schooling.
Our educational approach balances craft-based learning with theory, which helps students to develop a solid foundation to successfully initiate and manage their future career path. The faculty, the facilities, a dynamic atmosphere and the commitment to quality and productivity all guarantee that effective learning can take place.
Through its governing board, the Academy is well connected with key leaders from government, the private sector and professional industry groups. The Academy’s strong alliances with the leaders of established hotels and restaurants provide students unparalleled opportunities for internships, on-the-job training, and guaranteed job placements upon graduation.
A bright future for skilled and educated employees lays ahead. The World Travel and Tourism Council forecasts that Cambodia’s tourism industry will expand greatly in the next 10 years, creating an additional 130,000 jobs by 2020.
Through its affiliation with the Swiss Hotel Management School Lucerne (SHL) the Academy’s curriculum was developed in close collaboration with SHL, ensuring that Swiss standards for culinary and hospitality education are followed. The diploma gained by successful graduated students is acknowledged by SHL.
Find your niche in the tourism and hospitality sector.
