Find out everything you can about the development team
Several ICO’s are present in the market and each one is unique from one another. They promise enormous profits and feasible returns for their investors.
The Ethereum platform along with other cryptocurrencies is generally considered to be experimental in nature. Several popular ICOs depend on Ethereum and they follow an experimental mechanism.
The only thing missing from the project is a final product that is finished completely. You can have a Minimum Value Product or MVP so it can allow you to be aware of the initial viability of the project and help you assess if the project has a future.
For instance, EOS ran an ICO campaign without a product or even a platform and still managed to raise over $ 4 billion during its entire campaign. Their token started trading at $ 0.925 and was at around $ 5 for a couple of days after the launch of an ICO.
However, we do not suggest that you follow this seriously either. The creative mind behind Ethereum, Vitalik Buterin who is also the most prominent figure of the crypto world has highlighted this as the following:
To start off, ensure that the developers are not anonymous. It can be quite alarming if they are and if they disclose their names and identity, you need to do research online and focus on the development team behind the project.
A telegram chat or a public Slack can be a good sign for investors. Sources like Facebook, Reddit, and Twitter can also prove to be quite beneficial when you evaluate an ICO.
The team’s presence on social media and constant communication with investors is also a very good sign. Constantly communicating with investors and keeping them up to date also gives out a good sign for the social media presence.
Of course, it is always safer to invest in projects that are as close to the launch of a fully functional product as possible. As a general rule of thumb, investors look to prioritize projects that have a few lines of working code.
You could also look for Venture Capital investments. Venture capitalists that are well-built in the market usually comprise experienced players so they will avoid investing in a project where they believe they can fail.
BitcoinTalk.org will be useful when you decide to invest in an ICO as it is the largest forum dedicated to Bitcoin and everything related to cryptocurrency. Several announcements are made here and they are marked with an ANN.
In online forums or in the cryptocurrency community, importance is given to the user’s reputation. Each post in an online thread will contain the current ranking of the person and the number of previous posts.
The entire guide is a synopsis to know what exactly you will be investing in. Similarly, you can learn everything about the project by reading its white paper.
It can help you: What is a white paper and how to write it?
A white paper will have to answer questions stating why does a project needs its own dedicated token and why cannot cryptocurrencies like Ethereum and bitcoin be used?
We know that a legitimate project will provide its potential investors with a roadmap. So if it contains a detailed breakdown of how the funds raised will be used, the pricing model, and the value assigned to the business, it can give a good sign to the investors.
If you have even a little background in programming and are aware of how to read the code, you should do so when evaluating an ICO. You can understand a lot about a project and its developers simply by analyzing the code they have created.
You can learn several important things from venture capitalists. You can know what you are investing in, manage your risks and assess a company before you invest your money.
