An “airdrop” is a term used to describe a distribution of tokens or other digital assets to a large number of people, often without any pre-existing relationship. These distributions are often done in order to raise money for a new cryptocurrency or blockchain project and can be done through various means, such as releasing tokens through an online platform, giving away free coins through social media platforms, or holding airdrops during events like the Consensus conference.
There are a number of different types of airdrops, including those that require users to complete specific tasks before receiving the tokens, and those that offer tokens without any requirements.
