Most vegetables should be grown under 30 to 50 percent shade.
The key to success with shade cloth is to hang it high enough above the plants, and provide enough ventilation that heat does not build up beneath it.
Providing shade of any type can reduce the ambient temperature around your plants by 10 degrees F. or more – in some cases, enough to keep plants from going dormant in the hottest weather.
