What is the difference between cement self-leveling and gypsum self-leveling?
Cement self-leveling is a processed special material that is mixed with water to form a liquid substance with a certain fluidity, which relies on gravity to freely diffuse to form a horizontal plane, and naturally condenses into a floor construction method.
Gypsum self-retaining is a kind of dry powder mortar specially used for floor leveling, which is prepared by carefully configuring and mixing gypsum materials, special aggregates and various construction chemical additives in the factory.
Gypsum self-leveling : the thinnest thickness can be 3mm.
Cement self-leveling is suitable for sites that are often in contact with water and have small ground flatness errors.
The price of the two materials is not much different, about 15-30 yuan/m2, but during the self-leveling construction of gypsum, there is no need for secondary leveling, which will save a certain amount of construction cost in some sites.
How to choose between cement self-leveling and gypsum self-leveling?
a. If the site is often in contact with water or the site level difference is less than 5mm, use cement to self-level.
