Importance of Surface pretreatment for anti-corrosion coating operation News
TAA technical department believes that surface pretreatment plays the most important role in the performance of the coating.
Surface pretreatment is a basic work Surface pretreatment can create conditions for coatings with excellent performance in two aspects: in mechanical, it provides surface roughness for coatings; And in chemical, it makes the molecules of the coating in close contact with the surface of the steel substrate.
If the surface is smooth, there will be no good adhesion between the coating and the surface, and the coating on the surface can be removed effortlessly. On the contrary, if the surface of the workpiece is as rough as sandpaper, it is not easy to remove the coating.
The workpiece treated with non-metallic abrasive has no Fe atom residue and is not easy to rust and discolor, but it has high crushing rate, large dust and serious pollution, which does not meet the requirements of environmental protection. TAA stainless steel grit can well solve the problems encountered.
Stainless steel cut wire can prevent the workpiece surface from rusting and discoloration, but it will become round during blasting, so it can not meet the roughness requirements.
In addition, stainless steel grit can replace a variety of mineral sand and non-metallic abrasives, such as alumina oxide, emery, quartz sand, glass beads, etc.
News - Energy saving, Environmental protection, Safety, all you want to know about stainless steel grit is here!
Energy saving, Environmental protection, Safety, all you want to know about stainless steel grit is here! News
At present, for the surface cleaning of non-ferrous metals and stainless steel products, there are still many non-metallic abrasive being used (brown aluminum oxide, garnet, emery, glass beads, etc.). However, as the country’s requirements for environmental protection are getting higher and higher, workers’ occupational health is becoming more and more important.
Stainless steel gritis mainly used for surface cleaning, paint removing and descaling of non-ferrous metals and stainless steel products, forming uniform surface roughness, thus especially suitable for surface pretreatment before coating. Compared with non-metallic abrasives, stainless steel grithelp to reduce operating costs and dust emissions and improve working environment.
News - The principle and grade requirements of shot blasting machines sandblasting and rust removal
Rust removal is the use of compressed air to blast a certain size of grit on the rusted surface through a sandblast gun. It not only removes rust quickly, but also prepares the surface for painting, spraying, electroplating and other processes.
Dry sandblasting is very dusty, which is harmful to environment and people’s health;
In order to ensure that the steel surface reaches the required cleanliness and surface roughness after blasting, it is recommended to use angular or bead-shaped stainless steel abrasive with a grain size of 0.3-0.8 mm.
