The value of the nominal voltage often serves as type designation for surge protective devices for information technology systems. It is indicated as an r.m.s.
value of the maximum voltage which may be connected to the corresponding terminals of the surge protective device during operation. This is the maximum voltage on the arrester in the defined non-conducting state, which reverts the arrester back to this state after it has tripped and discharged.
The maximum discharge current is the maximum peak value of the 8/20 μs impulse current which the device can safely discharge.
